<h1>Rosita Chatonda</h1>
<p>Chicago Board of Education, District 10b, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Declared write-in.</p>
<p>These names are not printed on the ballot. To vote for one, write the name in the blank write-in space for that office and fill in the oval (on a touchscreen, follow the write-in steps on screen). Votes count only for write-ins who filed a declaration. The Chicago Board of Elections does not post those names, so this list comes from the Cook County Clerk&#39;s list and campaign announcements; election judges at your polling place have the official one.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Declared write-in candidate; the name is not printed on the ballot. No 2026 platform or campaign website found. In her 2024 write-in run for District 10 she called for equity for historically underserved neighborhood schools, an independent forensic audit of the CPS budget, and expanded special education services. She was removed from the 2026 ballot in July after the elections board upheld a challenge to her nominating petitions.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Chicago Public Schools math and science coach and founder of the Coalition and Alliance of Urban School Educators; she was a write-in candidate for the District 10 seat in 2024.</p>
